_ci07.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether congregation may set minimum voting age for elections","year":1984,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md:occ-a96bf8b26dea","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"The BCO provides no minimum voting age for congregational meetings, except where state law imposes one for corporate votes."}},{"id":"bco:24-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Definition of 'voter' in congregational officer elections","year":1982,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.md:occ-5256f35d92b4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga10_1982__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"A voter under BCO 24-3 is a communing member in good standing present at the meeting; only those who cast a ballot count toward the majority required for election."}},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Psiaki v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-b78e5434146c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":145},"excerpt":"…has not changed. The PCUS Constitution did not have a passage equivalent to BCO 24-3 in 1879, although such a provision, including the language “in good and regular standing,\" was added in 1925.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-e65efa46aca5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":163},"excerpt":"…and the first Stated Clerk of the General Assembly, wrote the following about BCO 24-3 (and, by extension 20-3):","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-a7d9d27abd4d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":167},"excerpt":"…does not include the phrase \"in good and regular standing,\" as he does from BCO 24-3, which does include that phrase, underscores the fact that he did not understand the phrase “in good and regular standing\" to convey any right to sessions or…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-7e5c4f3b7dc6","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":293},"excerpt":"The second phrase is “good and regular.” In BCO 20-3 (cf. BCO 24-3), “all communing members in good and regular standing, but no others, are entitled to vote in the churches to which they are respectively attached.\" Good standing focuses on those who are free…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-17a359acf28d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":331},"excerpt":"BCO 24-3 -- “All communing members in good and regular standing, but no others, are entitled to vote in the election of church officers in the churches to which they respectively belong\" [this provision governs the election of ruling elders and deacons]","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-2ae24e2069e1","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":401},"excerpt":"…regular standing” has persisted in our polity -now codified in BCO 20-3 and BCO 24-3 -- since its final adoption in 1879, now some 145 years in continuous use. The PCA has never changed it, having carried that phrase over from the PCUS in 1973.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-0a753d2fba6c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":433},"excerpt":"…can be regulated under the longstanding rules articulated in BCO 20-3 and BCO 24-3. Given that regulating minor communicant suffrage is not clearly prohibited by Scripture, was apparently accepted practice in Presbyterian churches since at least 1788,…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-733aa7539fa6","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":451},"excerpt":"…practice it, and were it not for the phrase “regular standing” in BCO 20-3 and BCO 24-3 together with the long history of local regulation of congregational elections in American Presbyterianism, the inductive arguments advanced would persuade us.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minor communicant voting","congregational meeting","voting rights","good and regular standing","church bylaws","officer election","communicant membership","BCO 6-4","BCO 20-3","BCO 24-3","BCO 25-1","age restrictions","session authority"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained Psiaki’s complaint and held that the CPC Session erred by ordaining and installing officers elected at a February 5, 2023 congregational meeting where the congregation’s bylaw excluded communing members under 18 from voting. Reading BCO 6-4, 25-1, and 25-7 together, the SJC ruled that all communing members are entitled to vote and that local bylaws cannot impose an age restriction; the “good and regular standing” language addresses censure, not age. The decision did not annul the completed ordination/installation, but required future elections and installations to comply with the Constitution."}},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Wilson et al. v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-315aeba3b485","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":485},"excerpt":"BCO 24-3. All communing members in good and regular standing, but no others, are entitled to vote in the election of church officers in the churches to which they respectively belong.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"},{"id":"bco:24-3--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-5f07fa81bceb","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":551},"excerpt":"…We must respectfully disagree with Morton Smith, who concludes that PCA BCO 24-3 requires that minor communicants be allowed to vote, on the ground that if they are able to choose Jesus as Savior then they are competent to choose their minister.…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["congregational meeting","minor communicant suffrage","voting rights","communing members","church bylaws","BCO 43-1 justiciability","associate pastor resignation","Covenant Presbyterian Church","Pacific Northwest Presbytery"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2022-20"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Members challenged a voting restriction imposed at a congregational meeting. The SJC dismissed the complaint as judicially out of order because BCO 43-1 permits complaints against acts or decisions of church courts, and a congregation is not such a court. It identified other possible routes through a report to Presbytery or review of church records. The adopted decision did not decide whether the voting restriction was constitutionally valid."}},{"id":"bco:24-3--overture:ga52_2025:22","record_id":"overture:ga52_2025:22","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 20-3, 24-3, and 25-1 to Permit Congregational Minimum Voting Age","year":2025,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga52_2025.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga52_2025.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-3--overture:ga52_2025:22:occ-557cb3963e36","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga52_2025.html#ga52-p1208","repository_path":"markdown/ga52_2025.md#ga52-p1208","locator":{"fragment":"ga52-p1208","page":1208},"excerpt":"","sources":["disposition_bco"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga52_2025.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 22 from the Pacific Northwest Presbytery (to CCB, OC)"}},{"id":"bco:24-3--overture:ga32_2004:2","record_id":"overture:ga32_2004:2","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 24-3 Regarding Election of Ruling Elders and Deacons","year":2004,"disposition":"Approved & ratified (2005)","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga32_2004.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga32_2004.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-3--overture:ga32_2004:2:occ-d26b0f4f5465","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga32_2004.html#ga32-p156","repository_path":"markdown/ga32_2004.md#ga32-p156","locator":{"fragment":"ga32-p156","page":156},"excerpt":"Amend BCO 24-3 Regarding Election of 